review_1906-07_SP_ballet_p011__b005.en:
On 29 April, to close the ballet season, the following were performed:  
1) “The Enchanted Forest,” a ballet by L. Ivanov and R. Drigo, with Mme Egorova (Ilka), MM. Kremnev (Iosi), and student Nijinsky (Spirit of the Forest);  
2) “Le Corsaire” (“The Animated Garden”), music by L. Delibes;  
3) “The Trial of Damis,” a ballet by Marius Petipa, music by A. Glazunov. Isabella—Mme Preobrazhenskaya; Damis—Mr Gerdt, soloist of His Majesty;  
4) “The Seasons,” a ballet by M. Petipa, music by A. K. Glazunov. Corn—Mme Preobrazhenskaya; Rose—Mme Trefilova; Bacchante—Mme Pavlova 2nd.

review_1902-03_SP_ballet_p011__b002.en:
In conclusion, a divertissement was performed, featuring Mmes O. Preobrazhenskaya, the ballerina of the Imperial Theatres of Moscow E. Geltsert, and the Honored Artist of the Imperial Theatres M. Petipa:  
1) The Jester’s Dance from the ballet “Mlada”—Mr Shiriayev;  
2) Pas de deux—Mme E. Geltsert and Mr Tikhomirov;  
3) Czardas from the ballet “The Enchanted Forest,” music by R. Drigo—Mme M. Petipa, Mr Lukyanov, Mmes Vasilieva, Slantsova, Pavlova 1st, Goncharova, Messrs Aleksandrov, Baryshistov, Fedulov, Gavlikovskii, Mmes Tsalisson, Ilina 2nd, Bastman, Sazonova, Legat, Pakhomova, Erler 1st, Shtikhling, Messrs Ognev, Berestovskii, Fedorov 1st, Lazuko, Ivanov 2nd, Ulanov, Smirnov 2nd, Trudov;  
4) Polka—Mme Trefilova and Mr Kozlov;  
5) Pas de trois from the ballet “King Candaules,” music by L. Minkus—Mmes Kyakshth, Karsavina, Polyakova;  
6) Matelote—Mme O. Preobrazhenskaya and Messrs Bekefi and Shiriayev;  
7) Mazurka, music by O. Rosenfeld—Mmes Sazonova, Ilina 3rd, Leonova 2nd, Chernyavskaya, Golubeva 2nd, Konetskaya, Georgievskaya, Spryshinskaya, Messrs Laboyko, Presnyakov 1st, Kiselev, Kristerson, Fremont, Baklanov, Presnyakov 2nd, Monakhov.  
The orchestra was conducted by Mr R. Drigo.

review_1904-05_SP_ballet_p015__b002.en:
On 27 February, to conclude the ballet performances before Great Lent, the following were presented:  
1) “The Pearl,” a ballet in one act by M. Petipa, in which the role of the White Pearl was performed by Mme Vaganova;  
2) Act II of “The Blue Geranium,” a fantastic ballet with music by Tsuni, newly staged by His Majesty’s Soloist G. Gerdt; “Grazziella,” a ballet in one act, composed by Saint-Léon, music by Pugni, in which the role of Grazziela was performed by Mme Trefilova;  
3) “Fiametta” (Act II), a ballet composed by Saint-Léon, music by L. Minkus. Choreography and staging by M. Petipa and Honored Artist of the Imperial Theatres L. Ivanov. The role of Fiametta was performed by Mme M. Kshesinskaya, Honored Artist of the Imperial Theatres; the role of Amour—by Mme M. Petipa, Honored Artist of the Imperial Theatres.

