The scenery for the ballet “Katarina” was painted as follows:  
First picture of the first act (“A wild spot in the Apennine Mountains, with a stream flowing in the distance”)—by K. O. Valts;  
Second picture of the first act (“Interior of a tavern near Rome”)—by P. P. Sergeev;  
Second act (“Salvator Rosa’s studio”)—by Mr. Groppius;  
Third act (“A square in Rome, with St. Peter’s Basilica visible in the distance”)—by K. O. Valts and Mr. Kakurin.

