review_1904-05_SP_ballet_p004__b003.en:
On 17 October, the following were performed at the same theatre:  
1) “Harlequinade”, for the 10th time; a ballet in two acts by Marius Petipa; music by Riccardo Drigo, with the roles performed as follows: Cassandre—Mr Gerdt; Columbine—Mme O. Preobrazhenskaya; Pierrette—Mme Egorova;  
2) “The Trial of Damis”, a ballet in one act by Marius Petipa; music by A. Glazunov; principal roles—Isabelle, Damis, and the soubrette Marinette—performed by Mmes O. Preobrazhenskaya and Vile, and Mr S. Legat.

